The '''Honor of Kings World Cup 2026''' (formally known as the '''Honor of Kings World Cup at Esports World Cup 2026''', Chinese: '''王者荣耀电竞世俱杯2026''') was the second edition of the tournament series, held as a midseason tournament for [[Honor of Kings]] in 2026.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/HoKEsports/status/1995059786560520621|title=It’s official — the 2026 HOK Esports Tournament Calendar is here|date=2025-11-30|author=HoK Global Esports|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> [[AG Super Play]] (participating as ''AG.AL International'') are the defending champions, but was defeated by [[Kuaishou Gaming]] squad 4-3 in the grand finals. Of note, the roster had 3 rookie players ([[WuYan (Zhao Haoyu)|silence]], [[XiaoYu (Wang Siqi)|Yu]] and [[LieFengFeng|LFF]]) and 1 player in their sophomore year ([[jHao|JuHao]]), averaging an age of 19.82 years old at start of tournament.

{{heroIcon|wang zhaojun|size=24px}} '''Princess Frost - Heavenbeacon''' was the commemorative skin for KWC 2026.

This year marked the first time a [[Honor of Kings]] tournament had been recognized directly by Garena since the original announcement for [https://www.facebook.com/ArenaofValor/videos/853059222265498 esports convergence] with [[AWC 2022]]. Champions of the 3 [[Arena of Valor]] leagues will be invited to the tournament, playing alongside teams from [[Honor of Kings]] leagues and beyond. A [[Honor_of_Kings_World_Cup/2026/Special_Version_Information|special version was used for the tournament featuring heroes from both games]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/HonorOfKings/status/2037350140546269625|title=Forged in Valor, Crowned by Honor. The road to the KWC at #EWC 26 is set!|author=[[Honor of Kings]]|date=2026-03-27|language={{flag|usuk}} English}}</ref>

On May 20, it was announced that the tournament, along with the entire ''Esports World Cup 2026'', was held in Paris, France, instead of the original venue of Riyadh, Saudi Arabia.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/EWC_EN/status/2057121960623006162|title=Esports World Cup 2026 is coming to Paris|author=Esports World Cup Federation|date=2026-05-20}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://esportsworldcup.com/en/news/ewc26-to-be-hosted-in-paris-france|title=Esports World Cup 2026 to be hosted in Paris, France|author=Esports World Cup Federation|date=2026-05-20|language={{flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> The [[KPL Dream Team]], winners of the [[Honor of Kings Invitational Series/2024/Midseason|HoK Midseason Invitational 2024]], returned to the Esports World Cup as a special guest for the tournament.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/i/status/2075429807857483943|title=The KPL Dream Team is coming to KWC at EWC26!|author=[[King Pro League]]|date=2026-07-10|language={{flag|usuk}} English}}</ref>

